# testkit — the testing tier (this product)

`contrib/testkit` is the test-support layer, imported **only from `_test.go`**
(its testcontainers engine never reaches the binary). Pick the cheapest tier
that answers the question.

## The five kinds of test in this repo

- **unit** — a function/component's behavior, hand-built, no container.
- **smoke** — "does it turn on": `testkit.Smoke(t, Modules()...)` — validate,
  boot, health, GET routes < 500, graceful stop, no leaks. See `smoke_test.go`.
- **sanity** — a targeted, fast (<5s), container-free assertion that a
  known-tricky invariant still holds. See `sanity_*_test.go` (`TestSanity_*`).
- **integration** — the wired graph against one real dep (`testkit.App` +
  a provisioner: `Postgres`, `Redis`, `S3`, `Sidecar`, …).
- **e2e** — the whole product boots and serves: `testkit.Scenario` (in-process,
  with actors) or `testkit.ScenarioProduct` (the real binary). See `e2e/`.

## Doctrine

- **Assertions**: `require`, not `assert` — the first failure stops the test
  instead of cascading. If you truly need two independent facts, write two
  tests. Use `go-cmp` (`cmp.Diff`) for deep diffs; keep kit APIs on `*testing.T`.
- **No mocking**: assert behavior, not interaction. Prefer recording fakes and
  real cheap infra (miniredis, in-process S3, a live pg database) over
  hand-mocked drivers. If a thing is "too big to fake", it is too big — split it.
- **No retries, bounded waits only**: drive `testkit.NewClock` where you can so
  there is nothing to wait for; otherwise wait on a condition with a hard ceiling.

Deployed smoke (post-deploy, over the wire): `testkit.SmokeDeployed(t, baseURL)`
— the same SPEC the `./{{.Name}} smoke --url BASE` builtin mirrors.

